## Provenance

This project is inspired by, and derived in part from,
[kimi-k3-in-c](https://github.com/FareedKhan-dev/kimi-k3-in-c)
(© Fareed Khan / kimi-k3-in-c authors), also Apache License 2.0. The upstream
checkpoint streaming design — pulling cold MoE experts from disk so a large
checkpoint never has to be resident in RAM — is the foundation this project is
built on.

Adapted from kimi-k3-in-c:

- `src/io/k3_st.c` / `src/io/k3_st.h`: the safetensors reader (header scanner,
  FNV-1a tensor index, bounded pread, O_DIRECT path, BF16/F16/F32 widening),
  extended with the DeepSeek dtypes (I8, I64, F8_E4M3, F8_E8M0).
- `third_party/tok.h`: the byte-level BPE foundation, extended with the
  DeepSeek-V4 pre-tokenizer family and the P/S Unicode table.
- `third_party/json.h`: the minimal header-only JSON parser (with a `json_free`
  tree walker added).
- `third_party/tok_unicode.h`, `third_party/tok_unicode_o200k.h`: Unicode
  category tables.
- The build-system structure and the streaming-cache engineering patterns.

Specific to this project (not derived from upstream): the DeepSeek-V4
architecture binding, FP8 E4M3/E8M0 and FP4 E2M1 quantisation kernels, YaRN RoPE,
Hadamard, Hyper-Connection, compressed sliding-window attention, the router and
expert batch prefetch, the memory planner, the prompt template, the verification
suite, and the downloader/doctor tooling.

